        "timestamp": 1777468843,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Mali junta chief makes first appearance since rebel attacks Issued on: 29/04/2026 - 15:20 Modified: 29/04/2026 - 15:21 Mali's military leader on Tuesday made his first public appearance since unprecedented large-scale weekend attacks destabilised his ruling junta, visiting the wounded and meeting the ambassador of key ally Russia. Jihadists and Tuareg separatists are still positioned in the vast Sahelian country's north, three days after launching a stunning wave of attacks, in what Moscow said remained a \"difficult\" situation. Social media abuzz as bees colonise bike outside the Louvre Museum 29/04/2026 'Decline' in press freedom: EU media landscape 'more concentrated, less transparent & less trusted' 29/04/2026 Europe King Charles III in the US : 'If it wasn't for us, you'd be speaking French' 29/04/2026 Americas Airlines worldwide cancel flights, raise fares amid Middle East conflict 29/04/2026 King Charles, Trump toast ties despite Iran tensions 29/04/2026 Ex-FBI chief Comey charged with threatening Trump's life in Instagram post 29/04/2026 Mali's embattled junta chief says situation 'under control' 29/04/2026 United Arab Emirates will leave OPEC in a blow to the oil cartel 29/04/2026 Indian billionaire's son offers home for Escobar's hippos 29/04/2026"
